content.text:
Now CSS for toolbar maybe `.toolbar-right` existing has flex no wrap; our appended rule with wrap overrides. Good.

Need index sort option `A–Z` uses en dash maybe fine.

Need add `data-info` handling on account page with auth-ui loaded and RUA98 ready. `infoContent()` calls RUA98.settings(), which requires db; init has likely occurred before user clicks. Maybe click very early before ready? auth-ui init immediately, RUA98.ready async; app.js/account.js await. If click info before ready, db may be null and settings throws. In practice RUA98.ready begins on auth-ui? Actually store.js loads, then auth-ui.js, then account.js awaits. RUA98.ready() not called by auth-ui. account.js calls it. If user instantly clicks after page load, likely ready. But could guard:
```
if (!RUA98.settings) return; 
```
or call openInfo after `RUA98.ready().then`. Better in openInfo: `RUA98.ready().then(() => { ... })`? RUA98.ready always returns promise. But synchronous click handlers then async. Implement:
```
function openInfo(key='returns') {
 injectInfoModal();
 const render = () => {...};
 if (window.RUA98) RUA98.ready().then(render).catch(...); else render...
}
```
But RUA98.ready returns promise and `infoContent` uses settings. Good. Yet openInfo currently synchronous used by product modal? It doesn't need sync. Fine. Let's modify to `Promise.resolve(RUA98.ready()).then(...)`. However `RUA98.ready()` already called and cached promise. Good.

```
function openInfo(key='returns') {
 injectInfoModal();
 const show = () => { content...; classes...; focus};
 RUA98.ready().then(show);
}
```
Need preserve key and trigger. Trigger set before promise. Good. If two rapid clicks, last? Both then. Fine. Let's do.

