content.text:
Now app.js changes. Let me write them carefully.

1. Add `recentGrid`, `searchPanel`, `searchInput`, `searchHint` consts.
2. Recently viewed functions.
3. Product modal share + deep link + push recent.
4. Stock flag in productCard.
5. Search extras handlers, aria-expanded.
6. Focus trap.
7. cart=1 handling.

Let me implement.

At top:
```js
const RECENT_KEY = 'rua98_recent_v1';
const searchPanel = document.querySelector('.search-panel');
const searchInput = document.querySelector('#search-input');
const searchHint = document.querySelector('#search-hint');
const recentSection = document.querySelector('.recently-viewed');
const recentGrid = document.querySelector('#recent-grid');
```

Recently viewed:
```js
function recentIds() {
  try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(RECENT_KEY) || '[]').filter(id => RUA98.product(id)); } catch { return []; }
}
function rememberRecent(id) {
  const list = recentIds().filter(entry => entry !== id);
  list.unshift(id);
  localStorage.setItem(RECENT_KEY, JSON.stringify(list.slice(0, 4)));
  renderRecent();
}
function renderRecent() {
  if (!recentSection || !recentGrid) return;
  const products = recentIds().map(id => RUA98.product(id)).filter(product => product && product.active);
  recentSection.hidden = products.length === 0;
  recentGrid.innerHTML = products.map(product => `
    <article class="recent-card">
      <button class="recent-media" type="button" data-details="${esc(product.id)}" aria-label="Ver ${esc(product.name)}">
        <img src="${esc(product.image)}" alt="${esc(product.name)}" loading="lazy">
      </button>
      <div class="recent-info">
        <div><b>${esc(product.name)}</b><span>${esc(product.subtitle || product.meta)}</span></div>
        <strong>${price(product.price)}</strong>
      </div>
    </article>`).join('');
}
```
Note event delegation: the recent section is outside grid, so add click listener on recentGrid.

Clear history button.

Deep link:
```js
function parseProductHash() {
  const match = location.hash.match(/^#produto=(.+)$/);
  if (match) { const id = decodeURIComponent(match[1]); if (RUA98.product(id)) openProductModal(id, { updateHash: false }); }
}
```
Open modal signature `openProductModal(id, options = {})`:
- after setting content: if options.updateHash !== false history.replaceState(null, '', `#produto=${encodeURIComponent(product.id)}`);
- rememberRecent(product.id)
Close:
```js
if (location.hash.startsWith('#produto=')) history.replaceState(null, '', location.pathname + location.search + '#colecao');
```
Wait: replaceState with '#colecao' doesn't scroll. Fine.

Share:
```js
function shareProduct(product) {
  const url = `${location.origin}${location.pathname}#produto=${encodeURIComponent(product.id)}`;
  if (navigator.share) {
    navigator.share({ title: `${product.name} — RUA 98`, text: product.subtitle || '', url }).catch(() => {});
    return;
  }
  if (navigator.clipboard?.writeText) {
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(url).then(() => AuthUI.toast('LINK DA PEÇA COPIADO ✳')).catch(() => AuthUI.toast(`COPIE: ${url}`));
  } else {
    AuthUI.toast(`COPIE: ${url}`);
  }
}
```
Note clipboard requires secure context; localhost is fine. Fallback maybe use a temporary input and execCommand. Implement robust:
```js
function copyText(text) {
  if (navigator.clipboard?.writeText) return navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
  const input = document.createElement('textarea'); input.value=text; input.style.position='fixed'; input.style.opacity='0'; document.body.append(input); input.select(); document.execCommand('copy'); input.remove(); return Promise.resolve();
}
```

Add share button in modal actions:
```html
<button class="product-detail-share" type="button" data-detail-share aria-label="Compartilhar ${name}">COMPARTILHAR ↗</button>
```
Place under actions or in trust area. I'll add below actions next to size guide? Put a row `.product-detail-extra` with size guide + share.
Currently `<button class="size-guide-link"...>` standalone. Wrap:
```html
<div class="product-detail-links">
  <button class="size-guide-link" ...>GUIA...</button>
  <button class="size-guide-link share-link" data-detail-share>COMPARTILHAR ↗</button>
</div>
```
CSS adapt: `.size-guide-link` margin-top 16px; wrapper. Let me keep simple: add separate button with class `size-guide-link product-share-link`, and adjust CSS `.product-share-link { margin-left: 16px; }`. But both are inline? buttons are inline-block by default; `.size-guide-link` has margin-top 16px each creating misalignment. Wrap in div with margin-top. Let me change markup:
```html
<div class="product-detail-links">
  <button class="size-guide-link" ...>GUIA DE TAMANHOS <span>↗</span></button>
  <button class="size-guide-link" data-detail-share>COMPARTILHAR <span>↗</span></button>
</div>
```
CSS `.product-detail-links { display:flex; gap:18px; margin-top:16px; } .product-detail-links .size-guide-link { margin-top:0; }`.

Stock flag in product card:
```js
const lowStock = !soldOut && product.stock <= 8;
...
${lowStock ? `<span class="stock-flag">ÚLTIMAS ${product.stock}</span>` : ''}
```
Place inside product-image maybe bottom-left. CSS.

Search:
- update hint in renderProducts? The hint should reflect current search result. Add `updateSearchHint()` called in renderProducts if search panel open or term non-empty:
```js
if (searchHint) {
  const count = products.length;
  searchHint.textContent = state.search.trim()
    ? `${count} ${count === 1 ? 'PEÇA ENCONTRADA' : 'PEÇAS ENCONTRADAS'}`
    : '';
}
```
- suggestion buttons click:
```js
document.querySelectorAll('[data-search-term]').forEach(button => {
  button.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.search = button.dataset.searchTerm;
    searchInput.value = state.search;
    renderProducts();
    document.querySelector('#colecao').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'});
  });
});
```
Should also close panel? Keep open? Close panel and scroll. Let's close.
- input handler already.
- keyboard `/`:
```js
document.addEventListener('keydown', event => {
  if (event.key === '/' && !/^(INPUT|TEXTAREA|SELECT)$/.test(document.activeElement.tagName) && !event.metaKey && !event.ctrlKey) {
    event.preventDefault();
    searchPanel.classList.add('open');
    searchToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded','true');
    searchInput.focus();
  }
});
```
Need `searchToggle` const.
- search toggle aria-expanded:
```js
const open = panel.classList.toggle('open');
this.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
```
- Escape resets aria-expanded.
- cart toggle aria-expanded.

Focus trap:
```js
function trapFocus(container, event) {
  if (event.key !== 'Tab') return;
  const focusables = [...container.querySelectorAll('a[href], button:not([disabled]), input:not([disabled]), select:not([disabled]), textarea:not([disabled]), [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])')]
    .filter(el => el.offsetParent !== null || el === document.activeElement);
  if (!focusables.length) return;
  const first = focusables[0];
  const last = focusables[focusables.length - 1];
  if (event.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { event.preventDefault(); last.focus(); }
  else if (!event.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) { event.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
}
```
Add in keydown handler before Escape logic:
```js
if (document.querySelector('.info-modal.open') || document.querySelector('.checkout-modal.open') || document.querySelector('.auth-modal.open')) return; // let auth-ui handle
if (productElements?.modal.classList.contains('open')) trapFocus(productElements.modal, event);
else if (document.body.classList.contains('cart-open')) trapFocus(drawer, event);
```
But this keydown listener currently only handles Escape; add at top:
```js
document.addEventListener('keydown', event => {
  if (event.key === 'Tab') {
    if (document.querySelector('.info-modal.open, .checkout-modal.open, .auth-modal.open')) return;
    if (productElements?.modal.classList.contains('open')) return trapFocus(productElements.modal, event);
    if (document.body.classList.contains('cart-open')) return trapFocus(drawer, event);
  }
  ...
});
```
But the keydown handler added later after DOM; fine.

Auth-ui focus trap: implement there separately for auth/checkout/info modals. Since app returns if any of these open, auth-ui handles Tab.

Cart focus restore:
```js
let cartTrigger = null;
function openCart() { cartTrigger = document.activeElement; ... cart-toggle aria-expanded true }
function closeCart() { ... aria-expanded false; if (cartTrigger...) focus; cartTrigger=null; }
```
Careful: openCart called after clicking quick-add from size picker, activeElement may be removed. Check `isConnected`.
Set toggle aria-expanded on open/close.

`?cart=1`:
```js
const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
if (params.get('cart') === '1') {
  openCart();
  const clean = new URL(location.href); clean.searchParams.delete('cart'); history.replaceState(null,'', clean.pathname + clean.search + clean.hash);
  AuthUI.toast('SACOLA ATUALIZADA ✳');
}
```
Call after initial render at bottom. Note: on load, cart may be empty; still opens drawer showing empty state. Fine but toast maybe "SUA SACOLA". Only if cart.count>0? Reorder always adds something unless all unavailable. I'll open if count>0 else toast "AS PEÇAS DO PEDIDO NÃO ESTÃO DISPONÍVEIS." Hmm the reorder page handles toast before navigating? It can't. Let's don't open if empty.

Deep link parse at bottom after render: `parseProductHash();` and `window.addEventListener('hashchange', parseProductHash)`? If user goes back, hash changes to #produto=... but modal closed; hashchange opens modal. And when closing we replace hash causing hashchange event -> parse sees #colecao no-op. Good. Add listener.

Recent render at bottom.

Also `renderRecent` on rua98:data.

Cart deep link: after render.

Let me now apply the edits to app.js.

