The issue: at load, `if (RUA98.currentUser()?.role === 'admin') enterApp(); else showLogin();` — showLogin resets form. If playwright fills before that runs (because await RUA98.ready() pending), then showLogin happens after fill and clears it. That's the race. Prior tests passed because CPU timing differed (or wait). It's a genuine (minor) UX race only under automation; in a real browser the user can't type within milliseconds before hydration. But we can make it robust by only calling showLogin after ready (it is after ready). The race is automation typing before the async IIFE completes. Not a real bug. To make tests stable, wait for app readiness before fill. For screenshot scripts, add waitForFunction that RUA98 && RUA98.ready resolved? Simpler wait 1000ms after goto before fill. I'll adjust screenshot script and previous tests don't matter.

But could a real user type during the ~50ms before hashing completes? Unlikely but possible on slow devices (hashing 4 users PBKDF2 could take 100-300ms). On a slow phone, user could type their email then it clears. That's bad UX. Better fix: avoid `form.reset()` when the form has user-entered values? Or delay rendering? Actually admin.js waits for RUA98.ready() before running showLogin (that's why it resets late). The initial HTML form is visible immediately while JS loads. A fast user or password manager could fill before ready. Fix: don't reset the form in `showLogin` if it's the initial render. Only reset after logout/login failure? Simpler: in showLogin, preserve values except when explicitly logging out. Add parameter `reset = true` and call `showLogin(false)` on initial. But social: after logout, reset makes sense. Let's change:

```js
function showLogin(reset = false) {
  ...
  if (reset) $('#admin-login-form').reset();
  $('#login-error').hidden = true;
  ...
}
```
And calls: sidebar logout -> `showLogin(true)`; initial -> `showLogin()`; enterApp failure -> showLogin() (shouldn't reset an attempt). This fixes race.

Also in the initial call, showLogin sets error hidden. Fine.

